# module CMake vendored integration adapter

Detect a consumer root `CMakeLists.txt`. This adapter applies only to a `cmake` export whose
dependency has a locked vendor; CMake has no native Git dependency form owned by this adapter.

# decision One generated include and one owned root line

Write dependency blocks to `deps/git-a2a.cmake`, sorted by module id. Each block calls
`add_subdirectory` for the locked vendored export path and uses the export name only as published
target identity. The root file gets exactly `include("deps/git-a2a.cmake") # git-a2a`; remove only
that marked line and only when the generated file has no dependency blocks. Never edit any other
CMake content.

# invariant Wiring requires explicit locked vendoring

Without both `dependencies[].vendor` and lock `vendor`, return a typed not-wirable reason. For a
submodule the source path includes dependency and export subpaths; for copy it includes only the
export subpath because copy already materialises the dependency module root.

# test Golden lifecycle

Fixture tests cover Wire, byte-identical second Wire, clean Drift, a changed generated block,
Unwire restoring the original root bytes, multiple sorted blocks, and the missing-vendor result.
Foreign bytes outside valid generated blocks are a drift finding; Wire discards them with a
warning and Unwire removes them without an ownership error.
